 in his way with  howard there's the added incentive of  scaring the hell out of jimmy and kim  and making it clear that if they don't  tell him what he wants to hear he won't  hesitate to get violent imagine a  scenario where jimmy tried to continue  the charade there's no way he would be  able to keep it up if lalo threatened  kim plus with everything else that's  going on there's really no way he could  let some random person walk out of their  apartment after the way they reacted  that brings us up to speed as far as how  we got to where the episode ended the  dead body in their living room has them  in a compromised position and jimmy  doesn't actually know enough to deliver  the proof that would satisfy the cartel  he knows about mike who saved his life  in the desert and that's basically it he  was under the impression that they moved  against lalo and took him out and now he  understands that that did not go as  planned kim has also met mike at this  point but she doesn't know much other  than the fact that he saved jimmy that  he's part of some organization that had  people following them and of course she  did know that lalo was alive but decided  not to tell her husband knowing all of  this they're gonna have to come up with  something because there's no reason for  lalo not to kill them after he feels  satisfied he's learned everything he  could from them that would be the course  of action that would make the most sense  if we didn't know saul survives to make  it out of breaking bad alive i'm really  curious to see how they make themselves  invaluable to him while managing to not  end up on the wrong side of mike and gus  when they come out on top it's going to  take drastic measures from everyone  involved that we know survives lalo is  smart he's cunning confident and  fearless he's borderline super  villain-ish and the only potential weak  spot we've seen is that he's ultra loyal  to his family all of this could work  against the character but he's 